        "original_id": "6a5f443b-7d7a-5f2d-849e-5b392c42a852",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Projects: One Manhattan Square, Time Warner Center, Hudson Yards Redevelopment Project, 247 Cherry\n- Companies: Extell Development Company, The Related Companies, AREA Property Partners, Apollo Real Estate Advisors, Skidmore, Owings & Merrill\n- People: Stephen M. Ross, David Childs, Mustafa Kemal Abadan\n- Places: Two Bridges, Manhattan, New York City\n\nFacts:\n- One Manhattan Square, also known as 227 Cherry Street or 250 South Street, is a residential skyscraper project being developed by Extell Development Company in Two Bridges, Manhattan, New York City.\n- One Manhattan Square is planned to rise 80 stories or 850 feet above the street and may include a new supermarket at its base.\n- 247 Cherry will be adjacent to One Manhattan Square.\n- Time Warner Center was developed by The Related Companies and AREA Property Partners, formerly known as Apollo Real Estate Advisors.\n- Time Warner Center was designed by David Childs and Mustafa Kemal Abadan of Skidmore, Owings & Merrill as two 750-foot twin towers connected by a multi-story atrium with upscale retail shops.\n- The Related Companies is best known for developing the Time Warner Center and the Hudson Yards Redevelopment Project.\n- Stephen M. Ross lives and works at the Time Warner Center.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "a2b4b80a-97bb-551e-98d6-8e135aa6d7a5",
